<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO raises KLM EPS forecasts.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO raises KLM EPS forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Research note summary (27/06)</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>KLM		 Airines	 60.20   ABN AMRO Hoare Govett</p>
<p>COMMENT: Hold (unchanged). Upgrades EPS forecast for 1997/98 and 1998/99 following upbeat meeting with company. Operational leverage strong and underlying developments more positive than expected. Cites operating profit target at least 400 million guilders in 1997/98 expected up from ABN AMRO estimate of 218 million. Firm dollar and higher load factors behind the upgrade.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     pvs EPS   P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996/7 (actual)   5.60    n/a	 10.8    4.0    1.00</p>
<p>    1997/8		5.43    3.95	n/a     n/a    1.50</p>
<p>    1998/9		6.27    4.56	n/a     n/a    1.50</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
